    <string name="recipe_carrot_rice">Carrot &amp; Chickpea Rice</string>
    <string name="recipe_chickpea_tray_step_1">Heat the oven to 200°C. Rinse and drain the chickpeas.</string>
    <string name="recipe_chickpea_tray_step_2">Cut the broccoli and carrots into bite-size pieces. Toss with chickpeas, olive oil and salt.</string>
    <string name="recipe_chickpea_tray_step_3">Spread on a baking tray and roast for 25 minutes, turning halfway, until the vegetables are tender.</string>
    <string name="recipe_lemon_chicken_step_1">Cook the rice in water according to the packet.</string>
    <string name="recipe_lemon_chicken_step_2">Cut the chicken into bite-size pieces. Heat the olive oil, add the chicken and salt, and cook, turning, until cooked through with no pink center.</string>
    <string name="recipe_lemon_chicken_step_3">Steam the broccoli until tender. Add lemon juice to the chicken and serve with rice and broccoli.</string>
    <string name="recipe_tomato_pasta_step_1">Cook the pasta in water according to the packet.</string>
    <string name="recipe_tomato_pasta_step_2">Finely chop the garlic. Warm the olive oil, add garlic, then chopped tomatoes and salt. Simmer for 10 minutes.</string>
    <string name="recipe_tomato_pasta_step_3">Stir in spinach until wilted, then toss with the drained pasta.</string>
    <string name="recipe_salmon_rice_step_1">Heat the oven to 200°C and cook the rice according to the packet.</string>
    <string name="recipe_salmon_rice_step_2">Place salmon on a baking tray with olive oil and salt. Bake for about 15 minutes, until opaque and flaking easily.</string>
    <string name="recipe_salmon_rice_step_3">Steam the broccoli until tender. Serve the salmon with rice, broccoli and lemon wedges.</string>
    <string name="recipe_chickpea_couscous_step_1">Prepare couscous with hot water according to the packet.</string>
    <string name="recipe_chickpea_couscous_step_2">Drain and rinse chickpeas. Chop the tomatoes, wash the spinach and crumble the feta.</string>
    <string name="recipe_chickpea_couscous_step_3">Fluff the couscous and divide into bowls. Add the vegetables, chickpeas and feta, then finish with lemon juice and olive oil.</string>
    <string name="recipe_carrot_rice_step_1">Cook the rice according to the packet.</string>
    <string name="recipe_carrot_rice_step_2">Dice the onion and carrots. Heat olive oil in a pan, add the vegetables and cook until the carrots are tender.</string>
    <string name="recipe_carrot_rice_step_3">Add drained chickpeas and salt, heat through, and fold into the cooked rice.</string>
